## Versions of mnist_*.py for various testing purposes
# mnist_basic.py
* Uses built-in nn.Linear
* Usage: python3 mnist_basic.py
# mnist_custom_linear_builtin.py
* Uses custom operator, but with built-in guts
* Usage: python3 mnist_custom_linear_builtin.py
# mnist_custom_linear_python.cpp
* Uses custom operator, but with hand-written python linear implementation
* Usage: python3 mnist_custom_linear_builtin.py
# mnist_custom_linear_cpp_builtin.py
* Uses custom cpp-based operator, but with built-in guts
* Usage: python3 mnist_custom_linear_cpp_builtin.py
# mnist_custom_linear_cpp_handwritten.py
* Uses custom cpp-based operator, but with hand-written c++ linear implementation
* Usage: python3 mnist_custom_linear_cpp_handwritten.py

## Note on updating the mylinear_cpp_handwritten_extension
Each time you edit mylinear_handwritten.cpp you must compile it by typing
python3 setup.py install --user
while in the mylinear_cpp_handwritten_extension folder

# Linear Implementation Libraries
mylinearPython.py
* Python implementation of the nn.Linear operator with custom python guts
mylinear_cpp_builtin_extension
* C++ implementation of the nn.Linear operator with the built-in guts
mylinear_cpp_handwritten_extension
* C++ implementation fo the nn.Linear operator with hand-written c++ guts

